## Why This Is Asked
Evaluates multi-language ownership, lifecycle management, and concurrency with CGO: opaque handles, per-handle state, and memory ownership across Go/C boundaries.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory ownership and freeing of malloced buffers
- opaque C handles and session lifecycle management
- per-session locking or serialized access for thread safety
- translating C error codes to Go errors
- resource pools and finalizers for leak prevention

## Code Example
